<h2 id="ha-ctrl-013-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Review owner, administrator and non-administrator views with permitted test accounts. Verify rejected actions at the backend independently of visibility.
2. Change an account preference and a client-only preference in two clients; record their actual persistence and sign-out behaviour.
3. Expire a session and revoke a permission while an edit is open. No rejected or unconfirmed change may be labelled saved.
4. Check keyboard access, private-field handling and shared-display scope. Confirm no token, secret or personal location appears in public evidence.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

